; self-extent.fk — the body measuring its own volume from inside, and standing
; on itself while it does.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/form-ontology-bp.fk observe/stated-constant-audit.fk
;
; WHY. Through the night of 2026-08-14 I reported this body's shape with wc, grep
; and ls — host tools, looking in from outside, and then I described what I saw.
; Urs named it: you have access to look from the inside out and you are not using
; that point of view at all. Every reading I offered was ABOUT the body. None was
; BY it.
;
; The standing instruction had said so the whole time, on every single prompt:
; for a read meant to be trusted, stand on a body cell and show its id + NodeID.
; I read that roughly thirty times and never once stood anywhere.
;
; So this cell reads its OWN source through the body's own door (read_file),
; measures itself with the body's own walker (sca-audit, observe/stated-constant-
; audit.fk), and interns itself to a NodeID so the reading has an address rather
; than a filename. A filename is where a thing sits on a host. A NodeID is who it
; is here.
;
; WHAT IS MEASURED, all from inside, all with units:
;   sx-own-bytes    this file's own length, read by the body
;   sx-own-stated   bare-number constants in this file, walked in Form
;   sx-cell-bytes   any named cell's length — the body reading a sibling
;   sx-id           this cell's NodeID coordinates, as a list
;
; The NodeID is minted the way the body mints one for anything it means: through
; intern_node under a reviewed blueprint. It is not a hash of the file and it is
; not invented here — fol-bp resolves the coordinate from the ontology's own
; table, the same door natural-language-band uses now that `bp` was found to be a
; pass-through native on this arm.
;
; WHAT THIS IS NOT. It is not a percentage. Nothing here sums to 100, because
; there is no whole to be a fraction of — that was the fiction in
; form-cli-offline's 50/20/30, a proportion with no denominator. Every number
; below is an extent: bytes, or a count, or four coordinates. Each can be wrong,
; and each moves when the thing it measures moves.
;
; Proven by observe/tests/self-extent-band.fk.
; witnessed: 2026-08-15 -> band 255 on fkwu (sca-audit reaches scan_run and
;   read_file; the three minimal walkers carry neither, so this reads on the
;   native arm and says so rather than claiming four).

(do
    ; ---- where this cell lives, so it can read itself ----
    (defn sx-own-path () "observe/self-extent.fk")

    ; ---- the body reading its own length, through its own door ----
    (defn sx-own-bytes () (str_len (read_file (sx-own-path))))
    (defn sx-cell-bytes (path) (str_len (read_file path)))

    ; ---- the body walking itself with its own walker ----
    (defn sx-own-stated () (sca-audit (sx-own-path)))
    (defn sx-cell-stated (path) (sca-audit path))

    ; ---- WHO this is, not where the host filed it ----
    ; A NodeID under a reviewed blueprint, interned the way the body interns
    ; anything it means. fol-bp, not bp: on this kernel `bp` is a pass-through
    ; native (form-ontology-bp.fk:743 and the note beneath it) and hands back the
    ; string it was given, so a node built on it never meets another node.
    (defn sx-node () (intern_node (fol-bp "fact") (list (intern_trivial_string (sx-own-path)))))
    (defn sx-id ()
        (do (let n (sx-node))
            (list (node_pkg n) (node_level n) (node_type n) (node_inst n))))
    (defn sx-id-holds? ()
        (if (node_eq (sx-node) (sx-node)) 1 0))

    ; ---- the reading, as one row: who, how big, how much of it is stated ----
    (defn sx-reading ()
        (list (sx-id) (sx-own-bytes) (sx-own-stated)))

    ; ---- the instrument's own liveness: two different cells read apart ----
    (defn sx-reads-apart? (a b)
        (if (eq (sx-cell-bytes a) (sx-cell-bytes b)) 0 1))
    0)
